{"content":{"result":[{"rank_order":1,"title":"How do I troubleshoot Amazon SNS publishing and subscription issues?","context":"### Grant another AWS service permissions to publish to an Amazon SNS topic\n\nYour Amazon SNS topic [resource-based policy](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/access_policies_identity-vs-resource.html) must allow the other AWS service to [publish](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sns/latest/api/API_Publish.html) messages to the topic. Review your topic's access policy to confirm that it has the required permissions.\n\nTo add the required permissions, [edit your Amazon SNS topic's access policy](https://repost.aws/knowledge-center/sns-edit-topic-access-policy) so that it includes the following permissions statement:\n\n```plaintext\n{\n \"Sid\": \"Allow-AWS-Service-to-publish-to-the-topic\",\n \"Effect\": \"Allow\",\n \"Principal\": {\n \"Service\": \"SERVICE.amazonaws.com\"\n },\n \"Action\": \"sns:Publish\",\n \"Resource\": \"arn:aws:sns:REGION:ACCOUNT-ID:TOPIC-NAME\"\n}\n```\n\n**Note:** Replace **SERVICE** with the AWS service name, **REGION** with your AWS Region, **ACCOUNT-ID** with your account ID, and **TOPIC-NAME** with your SNS topic name.\n\n**Important:** These permissions allow anyone that has access to your SNS topic's Amazon Resource Name (ARN) to publish messages to the topic through the service endpoint. You can add [global condition keys](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/reference_policies_condition-keys.html) to restrict the publishing permissions to specific resources.\n\nThe following example IAM policy uses the [arnLike](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/reference_policies_elements_condition_operators.html#Conditions_ARN) condition operator and the [aws:SourceArn](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/reference_policies_condition-keys.html#condition-keys-sourcearn) global condition key to restrict Amazon SNS publishing permissions to specific resources:\n\n```plaintext\n{\n \"Sid\": \"Allow-AWS-Service-to-publish-to-the-topic\",\n \"Effect\": \"Allow\",\n \"Principal\": {\n \"Service\": \"SERVICE.amazonaws.com\"\n },\n \"Action\": \"sns:Publish\",\n \"Resource\": \"arn:aws:sns:REGION:ACCOUNT-ID:TOPIC-NAME\",\n \"Condition\": {\n \"ArnLike\": {\n \"aws:SourceArn\": \"arn:aws:SERVICE:REGION:\n\n*[truncated — additional content omitted]*","url":"https://repost.aws/knowledge-center/sns-publish-subscribe-troubleshooting"},{"rank_order":2,"title":"AmazonRekognitionServiceRole","context":"## Policy details\n\n* **Type**: Service role policy\n* **Creation time**: November 29, 2017, 16:52 UTC\n* **Edited time:** November 29, 2017, 16:52 UTC\n* **ARN**:\n `[redacted ARN]`","url":"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/aws-managed-policy/latest/reference/AmazonRekognitionServiceRole.html"},{"rank_order":3,"title":"How can I make sure that I receive Amazon SNS notifications from AWS Config?","context":"### Grant your AWS account permission to publish your SNS topic\n\nYou must choose either a [service-linked role](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/id_roles_terms-and-concepts.html#iam-term-service-linked-role) or a custom role as your recorder role. The recorder role is an AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM) role that allows you to record configuration information.\n\n**Important:** As a security [best practice](https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/mt/aws-config-best-practices/), use the custom configuration service role as a recorder role. Avoid using the service-linked role as the recorder role for your cross-account topic policy. This is because the service-linked role requires you to set **\"config.amazonaws.com\"** as the **Service** property in your Amazon SNS topic policy.\n\nTo replace the Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the service-linked role with a custom service role ARN, add the following permission to the role permissions policy:\n\n```plaintext\n{\n \"Effect\": \"Allow\",\n \"Action\": \"sns:Publish\",\n \"Resource\": \"arn:aws:sns:Region:AccountId:Topic-Name\"\n}\n```\n\nFor more information on custom roles, see [Permissions for the IAM Role Assigned to AWS Config](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/iamrole-permissions.html)","url":"https://repost.aws/knowledge-center/config-sns-notification-troubleshooting"}]}}

